% Coverage for the "%%MIDI beatstring" directive in the golden test suite.
% beatstring assigns a per-beat dynamic (f/m/p -> loud/medium/soft note
% velocity) to each metrical position in the bar; note_beat() then indexes
% beatstring[] by beat position to set each NoteOn velocity.  With L:1/8 in
% 4/4 the bar holds eight eighth notes, one per beatstring character, so the
% "fmfmfffp" pattern maps onto the eight notes and pins eight distinct
% velocities in the rendered MIDI.
%
% This is also the regression guard for the heap-buffer-overflow that the
% beatstring parser used to hit at end-of-string (strchr matched its search
% set's terminating NUL, so the loop ran one byte past the directive text).
% Under the sanitizer build the overflow aborts abc2midi, failing this test.
X:1
T:Beatstring velocity control
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=120
K:C
%%MIDI beatstring fmfmfffp
C D E F G A B c |
